  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SP - Woord en Daad - Bee a Champion</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&#x2019;s long-term goal is to create a competitive and inclusive apiculture sector in Uganda in which smallholder producers, processors and service providers collaborate effectively to increase productivity and efficiency leading to improved revenues and an increase in jobs and incomes.

Overall, by creating a competitive and inclusive honey sector, the project works towards the goal to lower poverty levels (SDG 1: End poverty in all its forms everywhere) and towards new opportunities for employment by lowering the entry levels to start beekeeping as a business (SDG 8: Promote sustained, inclusive and sustainable growth, full and productive employment and decent work for all). Beekeeping enhances pollination and honey is a nutritious food product, both contributing to SDG 2 (End hunger, achieve food security and improved nutrition and promote sustainable agriculture). Beekeeping is a climate smart practice, and a rich biodiversity is necessary for good quality honey. Beekeeping requires conservation of bee species, tree resources and enrichment of flowering plants for pollination. This contributes to climate change mitigation (SDG 13) and a sustainable use of natural resources (SDG 15). The project focusses on gender equality as a cross-cutting issue (SDG 5) aiming at least 50% of participants as women.</narrative>
  </description>
